\f0\fs24 \cf0 Hey Max, \
\
The main script is the network_mip.gms file which requires the network_data.gms file to be located in the same directory. The network_data file contains the indexed parcel set optimized within the main network_mip file against the unit-treatment costs of the water treatment facility. \
\
The set of candidate parcels were calculated by a python script that took two main outputs from the InVEST model and calculated the most promising prospects. This file was prep_network_gams.py which took flow_direction.tif, n_total_export.tif, and places_reprojected_use.tif as inputs. The flow_direction file stores the flow-linkages of each pixel-unit into associated chains, and the n_total_export file stores the estimated nitrogen output of each pixel in the watershed. The third file, places_reprojected_use stored estimates of land value, and was projected onto this grid as another layer. The python script then aggregated the downstream nitrogen flows between pixels, and normalized them by land price to estimate the most economic pixel-units to purchase for nitrogen retention. I chose not to include the .tif raster files since they are upwards of 2 GB in size. \
\
Let me know your thoughts, \
Nate}